   959	///
   960	/// Why this exists: egglog has f64 primitives for `+ - * neg` only — no
   961	/// `ln`/`sqrt`/trig — so a transcendental constant subtree can NEVER fold in
   962	/// the e-graph, in any rule family. The evaluator has the real functions.
   963	/// This is the piece that lets `pi*(r^2 + log|sqrt2|) - 1.0888` reduce: fold
   964	/// the transcendental remainders to literals, then let the data-gated strip /
   965	/// prune drop what cancels.
